---
description: Behavior-changing commits need a PR; no-op pushes to main are OK if disclosed
alwaysApply: true
---

# When to create a PR

- For any commit that changes app behavior, schema, APIs, config that affects runtime, or deployables: create a branch and open a pull request. Do not push those commits straight to `main`.
- For no-op / non-affecting work only (Cursor rules, docs with no runtime impact, chore metadata): pushing to `main` is allowed. Always tell the user when you pushed directly to `main`.
- Prefer a PR whenever unsure whether the change affects anything.